\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ src/kernel.fam — the kernel, what the node boots.  One thread, one loop over
\ its devices: the kernel first (src/proc.fam kinit: the trap vector, the timer
\ and the PLIC
\ doorbells that `wait` needs), then every turn takes the frames in (those for
\ ports programs hold go to the programs: src/ports.fam; the kernel's own TCP
\ only answers strays), serves the programs' requests (src/ksrv.fam), and
\ sleeps until a doorbell or 100 ms.  The web server is prog/wm.fam on TCP
\ 8080 and the UDP echo prog/udpecho.fam on 3737, both in user mode.
\ The store (src/store.fam) opens on the disk 32 MiB in, past the boot image;
\ the programs appended to the image are installed in it (src/exec.fam) and
\ bin/init is exec'd: it runs the programs the store's "init" value names and
\ restarts what gets killed.  That list is the build's default (hello, crash,
\ udpecho and wm) until it is edited through the page's store box: a list the
\ node did not write is left alone, its own is replaced when the default
\ changes ("init.default" remembers what it wrote).
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

: pblob variable ;  : inl variable ;  : idl variable ;  : ibuf variable ;  : stok variable ;
: idef ( -- s n )  "hello crash udpecho wm" 16 lit ;
: isame ( a b n -- flag )  -1 lit swap 0 lit do 2 lit pick i + c@ 2 lit pick i + c@ <> if drop 0 lit then loop nip nip ;

0 lit alloc dup pblob ! progsize alloc drop                \ the programs blob sits at the heap base: keep it
40 lit 18 lit 8 lit kinit                                  \ 64 x 128 KiB, 24 x 1 MiB, 8 x 8 MiB of regions: 96 MiB
2710 lit quantum!                                          \ 1 ms slices: a program answering a packet is not kept waiting for the timer
evinit
evnet? @ if
	0A00020F lit FFFFFF00 lit 0A000202 lit ethinit drop
	evdsk @ if 10000 lit pgbase !  evdsk @ pgopen drop stinit  exinit  ksinit  -1 lit stok !  200 lit alloc ibuf !
		"q: store open, 32 MiB into the disk; " puts pblob @ proginst dup u. " program(s) installed" puts
		0= if " (no programs blob at the heap base " puts pblob @ u.x ": is the node loaded on a page boundary?)" puts then '\n' lit putc
		0 lit txbeg dup "init" 4 lit ibuf @ 100 lit get inl !  dup "init.default" C lit ibuf @ 100 lit + 100 lit get idl !  txcommit
		inl @ 0<  inl @ idl @ = inl @ 0< 0= and if ibuf @ ibuf @ 100 lit + inl @ isame else 0 lit then  or
		inl @ B lit = if ibuf @ "hello crash" B lit isame else 0 lit then  or                              \ the defaults of builds before
		inl @ 13 lit = if ibuf @ "hello crash udpecho" 13 lit isame else 0 lit then  or if                \ "init.default" existed
			-1 lit txbeg dup "init" 4 lit idef put txcommit then
		idl @ 16 lit = if ibuf @ 100 lit + idef isame else 0 lit then 0= if
			-1 lit txbeg dup "init.default" C lit idef put txcommit then
	else 0 lit stok !  "q: no disk: the store is off\n" puts then
	udpinit  pinit  8 lit tcpinit
	10000005 lit c@ 1 lit and if getc drop then               \ the 'q' scripts/boot.sh QUIET=1 sends after the boot config
	0 lit tlog !
	stok @ if "bin/init" 8 lit 20000 lit 5 lit exec "q: exec bin/init: thread " puts u. '\n' lit putc then
	begin
		evarm
		begin netrx while netin netrel repeat
		pdlv @ if 0 lit pdlv ! yield then                     \ a program got frames: let it answer now, the answers go out below
		ksturn
		tcptick
		10000 lit F4240 lit evwait drop                       \ bit 16: a program's request or exit
	0 lit until
else "q: no NIC, nothing to do\n" puts then
bye
